# fpu_synth.ys — prove every fpu.v module is truly synthesizable (no `real`, no latches, no
# combinational loops), independent of the iverilog bit-exact proof. `check -assert` fails loudly on
# any inferred latch / floating logic; `synth` maps to a generic gate netlist. Run one module at a
# time with: yosys -q -p "read_verilog -sv fpu.v; synth -top <mod> -flatten; check -assert; stat"
# or just: yosys fpu_synth.ys  (checks fp_addsub / fp_mul / fp_cmp / fp_div / fp_sqrt in turn).
read_verilog -sv fpu.v
hierarchy -check
proc
opt
check -assert
synth -flatten
stat
